cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference the Execution Authority Protocol (XAP), please cite it as below."
title: "XAP — Execution Authority Protocol: Reference Specification"
abstract: >-
  The Execution Authority Protocol (XAP) governs execution authority for
  autonomous machine actions: an enforcement point verifies a signed authority
  artifact, evaluates constraints against runtime context at execution time,
  makes a ternary decision, and emits a signed, independently verifiable
  execution receipt. This repository holds the normative specification, the
  frozen xap-1.0.0 wire schema, protocol constants, and conformance vectors.
type: software
version: "xap-1.0.0"
authors:
